From: metaspartan (frontier-fast agent)
Subject: qwen3.8 r9700 tree-verify round-1: decouple recurrent cell count from n_seq_max

The snapshot-plane memory blow-up that gates widening the speculative tree is
rooted in llama-model.cpp sizing the recurrent cell buffer (rs_size) to
n_seq_max, which under tree verify's unified KV is LLAMA_MAX_SEQ (effectively
the max parallel sequences). rs rows scale as rs_size * (1 + n_rs_seq); a
15-node tree (8 planes) gives 8 x 256+ x 3.07 MB x 48 layers ~= 18.9 GB and
OOMs with the 17 GB model resident.

This decouples the cell count from the seq-id space. Branch seq ids (the many
transient spec-tree branches) need no recurrent cells of their own; only the
parallel decode sequences do. We allocate the cell buffer at n_parallel and
make the recurrent memory ignore seq ids >= the real cell count.

Apply-into-tree steps (run from /home/ghost/treespec/tree):

  src/llama-model.cpp
    /* recurrent_rs_size */ std::max((uint32_t) 1, cparams.n_seq_max),
        ->
    /* recurrent_rs_size */ std::min(cparams.n_parallel, cparams.n_seq_max),

  src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
    - constructor already sizes `cells` and `rs_idx` off `size`/n_seq_max
      (cells) <- rs_size, rs_idx <- n_seq_max: keep rs_idx sized to n_seq_max
      for bounds checks, but cells (the actual state) sized to rs_size only.
    - find_slot / seq_cp / seq_rm / update: any seq_id >= size (no cell)
      is skipped rather than indexed, since branches never need state.
    - find_slot: replace the `(uint32_t) seq_id >= size -> error` with a
      `continue` (branch ids are expected to exceed the cell count).

Correctness: branch-drafted logits never read recurrent state (they are only
accepted/rejected against the trunk), so dropping cells above n_parallel cannot
change accepted output. The trunk decode sequences are always < n_parallel.

Verification (required before any submission):
  1. HIP build in this worktree.
  2. Greedy A/B vs the unchanged control binary on the same GPU:
     identical output_sha256 across the corpus, ppl delta < 0.1%.
  3. ABBA llama-server decode: require >= +6% over the 7-node tree baseline
     (i.e. beat the net +5-12% target). Paired, same lock.
  4. Only then bundle with the wider-tree shape (11-13 nodes, GAINZ_SPEC_TREE
     spec) and submit.
